;; tags: mem-ops, addressing
;; expect: 7
;; Base+immediate-offset addressing. Exercises LDR Xt, [Xn, #imm] with
;; the immediate inside the 12-bit unsigned-scaled range that the AArch64
;; encoding allows directly (no need to materialize the offset into a
;; temp register). x86 emits a single MOV r64, [reg + disp].
;; We store four values at consecutive indices and read back element 3
;; (offset = 3 * 8 = 24 bytes -- comfortably inside the immediate range).
(defun main ()
  (let ((buf (new 'stack-no-clear 'array int64 4)))
    (set! (-> buf 0) 1)
    (set! (-> buf 1) 3)
    (set! (-> buf 2) 5)
    (set! (-> buf 3) 7)
    (format #t "~D~%" (-> buf 3))))
